    "observer_investigate": {
      "answer": {
        "answer": "Based on the Cellerator documentation, the legal execution candidates in the PBMC3K forward benchmark consist of exactly one legal FMP1 SpMM schedule per tested request. The reported planner regret measures the performance gap over this 'legal set' (the candidates exposed in the built-in catalog) and is explicitly documented as not being a universal cuSPARSE comparison. The explicit documented limits for the benchmark include: it is a computational fixture with no biological or scientific claims; it tests widths of 1, 16, 17, 31, 32, 48, and 64; it uses reuse values of 1, 8, and 1024; it utilizes two deterministic value generations (an identity cast and a signed stress-value generation); it employs an independent CSR referee; and it is restricted to 512 observations/row destinations.",
        "evidence_packet_ids": [
          "pkt_8a048da4575a42f7abb2d2a47201ee44",
          "pkt_95aec2e0216249cd884dbdee125dc7b1",
